# Aggregating reads of a duplicate-bearing lake table that are exempt
# from scripts/ci/lint-lake-dedup.sh.
#
# Format: `<file>:<stellar.table>  <reason>`, one per line. The key is
# printed by the gate on failure, so an entry is copied rather than
# hand-derived. The reason field is REQUIRED.
#
# SHRINK-ONLY. Adding a line needs a `Baseline-Growth:` commit trailer
# naming this file (scripts/ci/lint-baseline-growth.sh), and a line
# whose site no longer violates is STALE and fails the gate until it is
# deleted.
#
# CURRENT STATE: 0 entries. The tree's one aggregating read of a lake
# archive — opTypeStatsQuery in
# internal/storage/clickhouse/explorer_reader.go — already collapses
# with FINAL, for the reason audit C2-12 recorded: a re-ingested
# operation leaves an un-merged duplicate part that inflates count()
# until a background merge. Keeping this file empty is the goal, not an
# accident.
